
The force component data has been imported from the local values recorded on the Raspberry Pi.
In the Influx data, we only had the total forces available. To enrich this, I aligned the data from the two different sources and applied linear interpolation where values were missing.

Due to the load cell setup during the testing days, the raw value of the 5th line was divided by two. Using this adjustment, I recalculated the total force, saved as gs_total_forces.

As a result, the gs_forces (Backline, Frontline, 5th line, and Total) are now imported and recalculated.

Additionally, I added a new column, calculated_total_forces, which is computed as:

calculated_total_forces = FLIGHT_SEGMENT_loadcells_force - gs_5th_line_kg

FLIGHT_SEGMENT_loadcells_force is the actual recorded value and should be considered the reliable reference.